    <<elseif _random == 2>>

        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Let’s have a big battle!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> suggests, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“We’ll go back and forth picking wrestlers and make two GIANT teams and whichever team has people left at the end win!”</span> You agree, though considering this is pretend, you fully expect <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> to win in the end. Naturally, since it’s his toys, he picks first. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> chooses his favorite wrestler, who also happens to be the champion, and gives a not so subtle hint that you should pick the main bad guy. This goes on for a little, with <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> picking most of the good guys and you most of the bad. Babyfaces and heels, as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> explains. <br>
        <br>
        You don’t really mind following his lead though, as your goal is to entertain the boy and he sees happy enough as the teams are decided. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Alright! So, this is a Regal Rumble! Which means that if you fall over the top rope and both feet touch the ground, you are out. Last man standing wins! Oh! And people only come in every few minutes. We’ll go back and forth between my team and yours.”</span> You nod along with <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span>’s explanation, the kid seems pretty knowledgeable about the rules of wrestling and you get a sinking feeling that he watches it often. <span style="Color: LightGreen">His dramatic commentary as the match starts is also incredibly cute.</span> <br>
        <br>

        <div id=choice2>
            <<link "Ensure Kayden’s favorite wins<br>">>
            <<replace"#choice2">>
            You play along with <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span>’s story, which is one of domination by his favorite. Though it isn’t as simple as ‘he wins’. Instead, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> seems to set up near impossible odds against him where he somehow manages to come out on top through sheer determination! He also performs his finishing move many, many times. <br>
            <br>
            It is little surprise when he wins, down to the last man on his team but still able to come out after being outnumbered. <span style="Color: LightGreen">But you don’t mind losing, especially once <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> starts jumping up and down excitedly on his bed to celebrate his victory, favorite wrestler in hand.</span> <br>
            <<socialChange "Kayden" 3 1>>
