            <<link "Ask him about his other favorite wrestlers<br>">>
            <<replace"#choice2">>
            As the match goes on, you ask for <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span>’s opinion on each wrestler. This does make the match go a bit slower, but <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> seems more than happy to ramble on about his vast knowledge of wrestling. It is like listening to Noah ramble about Owlman characters, as each has a long history of back and forths. There are also a few that change between good and evil a lot. <br>
            <br>
            When asked about this, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> shrugs. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“That’s just how wrestling works. Sometimes you’re good, sometimes you’re bad. You gotta do what you gotta do to win!”</span> You ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> if his favorite has ever been the bad guy, but he strongly denies it. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“No way! Even when he did bad stuff it was only because they did it first! He doesn’t need to cheat to win!”</span> <span style="Color: LightGreen">You laugh at his obvious bias. It is very cute.</span> <br>
            <<socialChange "Kayden" 3 1>>
            <<needChange "Fun" 5>>
            <span style="color:green">+Kayden Fun</span><br>
            <<set $HangOutNeed.Fun += 10>>
            <span style="color:red">-Kayden Energy</span><br>
            <<set $HangOutNeed.Energy -= 5>>
            <br>
            [[Continue|OC Miller House Twins Room]] 

            <</replace>>
            <</link>>
        </div>

    <<elseif _random == 3>>

        You look at the pile of wrestling figures and pick one with bright green shorts and a mask. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh, that’s the Masked Menace!”</span> He smiles, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Alrighty, let’s see who my champ will be?”</span> He thinks for a second, peering over the pile of buff dudes in either little trunks or 90s attire before making his decision. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“This one!”</span> He proclaims happily, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“This is Powerhouse Jobs and he’s undefeated! You have no chance!”</span> You both preform your entrances one by one, with <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> singing the music from memory as you try your best to mimic the moves he describes to you as you move your figure into the ring. <br>

